<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dutch East India Company</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as VOC, Vereenigde Oostindische Compagnie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> (VOC) was a chartered trading company founded in 1602, with powers to wage war, make treaties and govern territory in Asia. It was the main instrument of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">East Indies</a>, displaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> from much of the spice trade and served as a model and rival for the English East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Company of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company.jpg" alt="Dutch East India Company" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Himasaram · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Dutch_East_India_Company.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
